ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: capture.seq.ingest
display_id: SEQ-CAPTURE-INGEST
module: capture
title: Ingest a runtime session
summary: Reads new records from a session into scrubbed events, then closes finished episodes and writes them as episode memories.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: A hook says a session has new activity, the daemon catches up at start, a Codex file goes idle, or history is imported
operation: capture.op.ingest
participants:
  - id: worker
    is: [sys.daemon]
    label: Ingestion worker
  - id: records
    is: [sys.claude-code, sys.codex, sys.openclaw]
    label: Runtime session records
  - id: db
    is: [sys.home]
    label: Stack database
items: []
parts:
  - capture.seq.ingest.a
  - capture.seq.ingest.b
rationale: >-
  Ingestion only runs in the daemon so a hook never reads a transcript inside the agent's turn. A
  failure leaves the cursor where it was, so the next trigger resumes from the same place and no
  complete record is lost.
